      "observed": "The 74LVC1G34 buffer U4 is powered from the VCC net, which is the unregulated input rail feeding the LM1117 input, P-FET source, and pull-up resistors. Its output pin 4 drives the SCK net that is also connected to the +5V-powered ATtiny MCUs and external ISP/I2C connectors.",
      "expected": "A low-voltage CMOS buffer interfacing with +5V ATtiny logic should normally be powered from the regulated +5V rail, or another rail within the 74LVC1G34 maximum supply rating, so that its output levels are compatible with U2/U3 and the connected headers.",
