          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(description \"Single Buffer Gate, Low-Voltage CMOS\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "V_5V +5V 0 DC 5.0"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If VCC is the LM1117 input rail, it is likely above the 5.5 V maximum for the 74LVC1G34. U4 could be overvolted and could drive SCK at an excessive level, risking damage to U2/U3 or an external programmer/host and corrupting the SCK signal.",
      "confidence": 0.75
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The files show U4 connected to the unregulated VCC rail while the ATtiny logic uses +5V; for a 74LVC1G34 low-voltage buffer driving SCK, this is a likely power-rail/rating anomaly that can overvolt the SCK net."
